# 220: step (a) precedes step (b) (§6 `.35`), because bytecode forces it — the
# VM has pushed the arguments before it can look at the callee. So a failing
# argument to a function that does not even exist reports `divide by zero`, not
# `undefined function 'nope'`. A tree-walker that resolved the name first would
# diverge here, and this case is the reason the order is pinned rather than left
# to each engine's most natural shape.
--- source
print nope(1 / 0);
--- expect
error: Value at line 1: divide by zero
